## What each outcome changes in the paper

| Outcome | Framework | Elsewhere |
|---|---|---|
| A: reversal survives exclusion | Keep 3.3, Prop 1(i) | Footnote flag shares in 5.2 |
| A: reversal collapses | 3.3 reads lost grants as "accounts that leave or are removed" | Rewrite 5.2's test paragraph; 7.1 second finding softened |
| B: price | Keep current file | 4.5: delete "does not fit" sentence, add the group-slope result; 7.2 "The cost" rewritten; Pope–Schweitzer to footnote |
| B: merit | Revert to gap-in-mu, kappa as price | 4.5 unchanged; 7.2 "The cost" unchanged |
| B: uninformative | Run D; price paragraph written as conjecture | — |
| C: floor found | Gate evidenced; cite from 3.2 | New paragraph in 5.1 |
| C: no floor | Gate dropped; receipt = b-shift only | 1.1 reciprocity framing stays; 3.4 shortened |
| E: PG ≈ 0, NC > 0 | Gate leads 3.4 | 7.2 "bundles" paragraph resolved toward learning |
| E: PG > 0 | Both channels kept | 1.1 unchanged |
| F: persistence established within both states | Allow persistent heterogeneity in both behaviors; assess selective versus general granting using cross-state and selectivity results | Expand persistence subsection with C/N and C/L estimates |
| F: only one state's persistence established, other imprecise | Limit claims to the supported state; leave the other unresolved | State which opportunities underlie the persistence claim |
| F: competitive-minus-noncompetitive contrast persists | Stable state selectivity is supported descriptively, without identifying a preference primitive | Report the year-to-year selectivity correlation |

Compute: A and C are cheap (account-level). B is one regression on roughly 1–2M rows with chooser FE plus the robustness set. D requires extracting casual games from the dumps, the only new data pull. E reuses the Section 6 pipelines. F uses existing opportunity data: one aggregation pass, cross-fitted composition adjustment, and account-level summaries/bootstraps. It requires no new API requests or Stockfish evaluations. Save the account-state-year panel so the raw and forward-prediction results need not wait for the adjustment fits.
